Answer: In the Daily Mail article, Professor Paul Lehner’s exact statement is reported as: “You’ll get it when you’re young, and not get sick. People will be invited to parties - like chicken pox parties - so you don't get it when you're older - but we’ll have to wait and see!” The article provides significant context and caveats, noting that this possibility was raised only “if a coronavirus vaccine does not come to the rescue,” that public health officials warn that parents are “playing with fire” by exposing children to potentially life-threatening infections, and that the broader discussion at the Science Media Centre press conference emphasized herd immunity as a last resort, with other scientists stating that vaccination is clearly the preferred approach.

